{
    desc => '2o opens 2 new lines below',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/count_open_2o`

Tests that `2o` opens two blank lines in insert mode, and typed text is
placed on each new line.

Keys: `2o` then type `new` then `Escape`

- **count_open_2o_initial.png**: Three lines of text, cursor at line 1 col 0.
- **count_open_2o_inserting.png**: In insert mode on first new blank line, showing "new" being typed.
- **count_open_2o_after_escape.png**: Two new lines inserted (each containing "new"), buffer now has 5 lines. Cursor on the second inserted line.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('2o');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->type('new');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('inserting');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_escape');
    },
}
__DATA__
line one
line two
line three
